Tue Sep 22 14:30:55 UTC 2026 - Nassim Lhadj <lhadjnassim311@gmail.com>

- Update to 6.1.1:
  - Changes in 6.1.1:
    * Theme: follow the desktop light/dark preference via
      the desktop portal
    * Reconnect automatically after resume
    * Spell check: list every bundled dictionary in settings
    * Open WhatsApp channel links and text-only send links
  - Changes in 6.1.0:
    * Add interface translations, selectable in settings
    * Show unread count as a launcher/taskbar badge
    * Allow spell check to use multiple languages at once
    * Add advanced option to render at the display's refresh rate
    * Tray: centre and size the monochrome glyph correctly
    * Wayland: match the snap-exported desktop ID so the app groups
      correctly
  - Changes in 6.0.4:
    * Spell check: fix dictionaries silently failing to load
    * Spell check: allow adding languages from spell check settings
    * NVIDIA/Wayland: fall back to software rendering instead of
    a black screen
  - Changes in 6.0.3:
    * Drag-and-drop: show a drop hint and report files that
      can't be attached
    * Tray tooltip now reads "Whatsie"
    * Bug-report diagnostics include the CPU architecture
  - Changes in 6.0.2:
    * Add a JavaScript memory limit to bound WhatsApp Web's heap
    * Open WhatsApp group-invite links in the join preview
  - Changes in 6.0.1:
    * Debian packaging for the Qt6 rewrite.
    * Fixes device linking (phone number and QR code).
  - Changes in 6.0.0:
    Major release and complete rewrite using Qt6 and QtWebEngine
    * Add light, dark and system themes
    * Add interface scaling and page zoom controls
    * Add message blur with configurable strength
    * Add application locking on startup, hide and idle timeout
    * Add isolated profiles with separate sessions, settings and cache
    * Add system tray integration and start-minimized option
    * Add desktop notifications with portal and tray fallback support
    * Add contact avatars to desktop notifications
    * Add downloads hub and spell checking sections
    * Add global and in-app keyboard shortcuts
    * Add Settings entry to the WhatsApp Web navigation rail
    * Set "Whatsie" as the linked-device name
    * Add GPU backend fallback and recovery handling
    * Add diagnostic bug reporting with crash information
    * Inject WhatsApp Web modifications using stable page structure
      instead of obfuscated class names
    * Add unit tests
    * Split application into core, web, platform, ui and app

